    {
      "id": "F9",
      "statement": "What separates the six alerts, which look similar as indicators (6 to 8 senders, one hour each): (a) onward-link depth runs 0 (A-28137), 1 (A-20636, A-85921), 3 (A-10859), 4 (A-37573) and 5 (A-83577). (b) The shape differs: one branch in A-10859 ends at two accounts, two parallel paths over the same accounts in A-37573 end at one account, and A-83577 has a single linear path. (c) Devices: the deeper three each have a device that sent from two or more of their path accounts (D-79802, D-45880, D-40018). The shallow or empty three have none. D-45880 is the strongest case, with one device behind every onward transfer from 4 path accounts. (d) A-28137 has no onward links at all, so for it there is no recorded relationship beyond the fan-in itself. All of this traces back to recorded transfers, links and device fields (traceable provenance), but none of it establishes fraud, common control or the movement of the same funds.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "R1",
