  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "id": "H1",
      "statement": "In alert A-37573, one device (D-45880) sends a quick series of onward transfers through four accounts, each a few minutes after the credit before it and slightly smaller. This could fit the four accounts being operated together, as in a layering pattern. The data records only the device field and the timing. It does not establish who controlled the accounts or that the same funds moved.",
      "references": [
        "S2",
        "P2",
        "P3",
        "R2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "H2",
      "statement": "In alerts A-10859 and A-83577, a device is shared by path accounts (D-79802 and D-40018). This could point to a common operator on parts of those paths. D-40018 is also used by an off-path account (A-34114), which may instead suggest a shared or public device.",
      "references": [
        "S1",
        "S3",
        "E17"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "H3",
      "statement": "Alert A-28137 has no onward links and no shared device on its route. It may be benign collection activity, such as small payments from many senders. A-20636 and A-85921, each with a single onward hop, may be similar. The data does not establish this either way.",
      "references": [
        "R6",
        "R4",
        "R5",
        "X3",
        "X4",
        "X5"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "unresolved": [
